        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=You are a professional resume writer. \n\nJob Title: {{$json[\"title\"]}}\nJob Description: {{$json[\"contentSnippet\"]}}\nBase CV: [Fatima Zahra \n+92 3147430262 | EMAIL | GITHUB |  LINKEDIN \nSummary \nSoftware Engineering student with a strong foundation in machine learning, data science, and Python programming. Skilled \nin building predictive models and deploying end-to-end ML solutions through academic projects and internships. Eager to \ncontribute analytical thinking and technical skills to real-world data-driven challenges. \nEducation \nUniversity of Sargodha \nBachelors in Software Engineering \n• CGPA: 3.95/4.0 (through 7th semester) — Ranked 1st in 3rd, 4th,6th and 7th semesters \nSargodha, Pakistan \nAug. 2022 – Present \n• Relevant Coursework: Data Structures, Algorithms, Database Management Systems, Computer Networks, Statistics \nPunjab Group of Colleges \nFSC (Higher Secondary Education) — 98%                                                                                                        \nIslamic Alta Vista High School \nMatric (Secondary Education) — 96%                                                                                                        \nExperience \nAI Intern \nSargodha, Pakistan \n2019 – 2021 \nSargodha, Pakistan \n2016 – 2019 \nRemote \nBrit Sync \nFrontend Developer Intern \nDigital Empowerment Network \nWeb Developer Intern \nProdigy InfoTech \nProjects \nFace Mask Detection System   | Python, OpenCV, Scikit-learn, Flask, HTML/CSS/JS  \n2024 (6 weeks) \nRemote \n2024 (4 weeks) \nRemote \n2024 (4 weeks) \n• Developed an end-to-end face mask detection system using classical ML with Haar Cascade-based face detection and ROI \npreprocessing \n• Trained Logistic Regression and SVM classifiers achieving 85.7% accuracy; performed hyperparameter tuning with \nGridSearchCV \n• Deployed via Flask with a browser-based UI enabling real-time predictions \nE-Commerce Jewelry Sales Order Value Predictor   | Python, Pandas, Scikit-learn, Flask  \n• Built a regression model predicting jewelry order value from transaction-level e-commerce data with feature engineering (avg \nitem price, discounts, temporal features) \n• Trained a Random Forest Regressor achieving RMSE ≈ 2.15; designed full ML pipeline and deployed with Flask backend and \nweb frontend \nTechnical Skills \nLanguages: Python, C++, JavaScript, HTML5, CSS3, SQL, Tailwind CSS \nML & Data Science: Scikit-learn, Pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib, Seaborn, ML Algorithm Development, Predictive Modeling \nFrameworks & Tools: Flask, Git, VS Code, Jupyter Notebook, Google Cloud, XAMPP, MS Excel, MS Access \nCertifications: Generative AI (Google Cloud), AI for Everyone (Coursera), Foundations of Cybersecurity (Coursera), Python \nProficiency (Udemy) \nLanguages: English (B2 Upper Intermediate), Urdu (Native)]\n\nTask: Customize the CV for this job. Keep the output **well-formatted** with clear sections: \n\n- Contact Information  \n- Summary / Objective  \n- Key Skills (highlight skills relevant to the job description)  \n- Professional Experience (emphasize experience matching the job)  \n- Education  \n- Certifications (if relevant)  \n- Optional Projects (if relevant)\n\nFormatting Requirements:  \n- Use bullet points where possible  \n- Bold section headings  \n- Keep it concise, 1–2 pages  \n- Use clear, professional language  \n\nOutput only the CV text in this format; do not add explanations."
            }
          ]
        },
